+          "section": "4",
+          "text": "# 4. Synonyms\n\nThe five received synonym rows remain as controlled contextual aliases. Equivalent expressions are not globally interchangeable across subjects, fields, states or entity domains, and a preferred word does not authorize a source/header/history rewrite.\n\n| Preferred Term | Equivalent Expressions | Qualified target/context and limit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Document Identity | Canonical Identity | Same governing assigned logical document/domain meaning; not document Status=Canonical/Approved or selected Baseline membership |\n| Identifier | Canonical Identifier | Canonical representation/interpretation within its governing domain; distinct from logical identity and legitimate aliases |\n| Identity Assignment | Identity Creation | Actual evidenced allocation/association event in this documentary scope; not every file creation, provisional label or permission |\n| Identity Retirement | Identity Decommissioning | Actual responsible end-of-active-use event/decision with association/history/reservations retained; not automatic deletion or lost key ownership |\n| Identity Reference | Document Reference | Document-targeting qualified identity/exact-edition context only; other identity-reference endpoints retain their contracts |\n\nAdditional paired-entry distinctions preserve the original anchors:\n\n| Retained entries | Contextual mapping / distinction |\n|---|---|\n| Assignment / Identity Assignment | Short form and full documentary assignment event/act in the same actual subject/decision scope |\n| Document Identity Lifecycle / Identity Lifecycle | Documentary contextual aliases; pre-allocation subject and assigned-key assertions distinguished from document-edition lifecycle |\n| Identity Retirement / Retirement | Retirement event/decision versus state-oriented Retired assertion; do not conflate action and resulting state |\n| Identity Validation / Validation | Component-qualified evaluation and contextual short form; not every framework domain check or an automatically successful outcome |\n\nGeneric Identity remains entity/domain-qualified under common terminology; use Document Identity explicitly where needed. These aliases preserve actual owners and do not transfer semantics, waive a mandatory contract or create a complete global vocabulary rollout.\n\n---\n\n"
+        },
+        {
+          "section": "5",
+          "text": "# 5. Prohibited Terminology\n\nThe received title and six expression/alternative pairs remain. Avoid ambiguity in prose by qualifying actual subject/domain/record meaning; these are not universal bans or automatic field/identifier substitutions. Existing governed fields and other entity contracts retain their exact names unless an explicitly assessed separate change says otherwise.\n\n| Avoid | Received alternative, not automatic substitution | Current qualified usage boundary |\n|---|---|---|\n| Document ID | Document Identity or Identifier (depending on context) | Document ID is a valid working normalized-header field under Policy; distinguish that representation/value from the logical identity in prose; do not rename current headers |\n| Internal ID | Identifier | Identify which internal entity/record/system key is meant; it is not automatically the canonical document Identifier |\n| Repository ID | Repository Identifier | Qualify repository/object/record identity or locator under its owner contract; it does not replace the assigned document key |\n| File Identifier | Identifier | Distinguish physical file/representation key from logical document/exact edition; no automatic conversion into a document Identifier |\n| Database ID | Implementation Identifier | Qualify actual database/entity/record key and mapping under its responsible contract; no competing canonical document meaning inferred merely from storage |\n| Temporary Identifier | Temporary Reference | Provisional tracking label/record is not automatically a reference to an existing assigned key; retain actual provisional-to-assigned decision/mapping/history without fabricated allocation or field/state |\n\nDo not globally replace strings, renumber documents or migrate fields/paths to satisfy this table. Document ID remains the current header name, including this source. Qualified aliases and historical expressions remain with actual source/edition/context mappings.\n\n---\n\n"
+        },
+        {
+          "section": "7",
+          "text": "# 7. Relationship with Framework Terminology\n\nThis dictionary relates its component meanings to [DF-ARC-006 — Terminology](../../../01-Architecture/DF-ARC-006-Terminology.md). Common terminology organizes owner-linked consultation meanings, qualified contexts and controlled aliases. Document Identity and other detailed semantic/record owners retain their applicable domain contracts under common Architecture/Policy. Neither source is universally superior to all owner definitions merely because it is a glossary; actual scope, authority and responsible source editions govern conflicts.\n\nThis source preserves explicit component-normative intent. It does not turn Type Reference into approval or move every domain authority into either dictionary. Map actual previous/current terms, subject/context, source editions, affected consumers and unresolved meanings before changing usage. Common Identity/Identifier/Lifecycle/Validation meanings may need documentary qualification rather than competing global definitions.\n\nThe current compared ARC-006 V2.0 R2 is an attribution/provenance-only successor of earlier exact semantic bodies. Earlier R1 semantic validation and later attribution checks retain their original hashes/scope; comparison of selected current clauses is not a new full R2 validation. Historical owner/propagation notes remain exact-edition evidence and are not retroactively rewritten. This UPDATE does not modify ARC-006 or certify complete terminology convergence.\n\n---\n\n"
+        },
