+          "section": "9",
+          "text": "# 9. Summary\n\nThe dictionary retains thirty original terms, including unnumbered Non-Reusability, with scoped component-normative meanings, actual owner/source responsibility, qualified aliases and evidence boundaries. Common vocabulary, detailed domain contracts, valid working field names, logical identity, records, exact editions, lifecycle assertions and operational decisions remain distinguishable.\n\nActual mandatory State/Canonical Reference/lifecycle complete-record authority, DID-014§14 additive/backward-compatible/core-not-extensible restriction and full terminology/consumer integration remain pending owner work. The selected Model/Schema/key view does not waive those requirements or invent an accepted merged state record. Ordinary compatible additions differ from necessary assessed normative revision under common Architecture AP-015–018 and DID-011§9; the actual restrictive peer contract is retained pending reconciliation, not silently repealed.\n\nThe functional DID README states: “The Document Identity component depends on the Metadata component for the canonical definition of metadata concepts used to describe document identity.” Current DID-009§5.1.1/§10 retains Document Identity→Metadata alongside Metadata→Document Identity. Keep both actual required claims pending responsible core-versus-descriptor/interface/source-edition reconciliation. Common required direction is consumer→provider with explicit contracts/scopes/interfaces under ARC-004/005; projection, navigation relabelling or glossary naming cannot dissolve a real required cycle or establish a complete globally acyclic graph.\n\nBefore a necessary term/owner/normative/domain/representation transition:\n\n1. Preserve actual original artifacts, source/rule editions, observations and failed checks; identify prior/new meaning, intended subjects/domains, rationale/alternatives, responsible authority and affected consuming sources.\n2. Assess exact semantic/record owners, consumers and indispensable interfaces, mandatory field/lifecycle/extension and actual reciprocal/cycle claims. Reconcile conflicting governing authority before broader conformity; do not rename away a required edge or presume all sources agree.\n3. Record compatibility, exact old→new term/key/alias mappings, domain qualification, collision/reservation/history evidence, same-document continuity and intended reference/exact-edition/pinned-snapshot effects. Preserve allocated/retired non-reuse and immutable historical selections; no arbitrary key reassignment or silent target/history rewrite.\n4. Apply only the separately authorized scoped change with actual contributor/event provenance, appropriate Version/Revision/history and coordinated transition evidence. Compatible working-document correction retains Version, compatible additive capability increments minor, incompatible contract/convention change increments major and resets minor to0; every persisted changed edition increments Revision monotonically across Versions. Other entity allocation/lifecycle rules remain separate.\n5. Validate the resulting exact artifacts/editions in the subsequent appropriate operation and report actual checks, executor, observations, coverage and remaining owner/consumer limits. Unchanged-source validation changes neither coordinate; later changed bytes require new assessment. Do not rewrite earlier pending/failure events as historical success.\n\nA definition, authorship, local PASS or semantic ownership grants no allocation, mutation, operational permission or formal approval. This UPDATE executes no terminology rollout, identity/domain migration, assignment, retirement, running resolver, security mechanism, publication or Baseline selection. Its own VALIDATE DOCUMENT has not yet occurred; the working successor remains Draft/Baseline Not assigned.\n\n---\n\n"
